    "status": "no-uk-product",
    "note": "No UK product information found for this combination. The clinic product is a cream with two active substances, dexpanthenol 5% and chlorhexidine dihydrochloride 0.5%. Searched 2026-10-17: emc lists dexpanthenol as an active substance only in an intravenous multivitamin, a decongestant nasal spray and a vitamin B syrup; MHRA products full-text search for dexpanthenol found no skin product with it as an active substance. The closest UK product (a chlorhexidine dihydrochloride 0.5% w/w cream) has chlorhexidine as its only active substance and lists dexpanthenol only as an excipient, in an unstated amount, so it is not the same product and was not used. Check the clinic pack for contraindications and allergy warnings."
